        "ai_gen_block_0029bb1_HyCk9p": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_0029bb1",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Gemological Institute of America (GIA)",
            "text": "<p>The Gemological Institute of America (GIA): Founded in 1931, the GIA is a non-profit, public-benefit organisation globally recognised for its leadership in gemmological research.</p><p>Through ongoing discoveries, the GIA continues to expand knowledge of gemstones and their characteristics. It plays a critical role in protecting consumers through rigorous analysis, education, and grading services, while establishing internationally recognised standards. The GIA independently verifies the origins of many of WILLIAM ÉDOUARD’s diamonds and gemstones.</p><p>The GIA also introduced a standardised carat weight system, designed to ensure precision and consistency in diamond grading. This scale typically ranges from 0.01 to 10 carats, with each increment reflecting a defined weight category.</p><p>When selecting a diamond, certification remains essential in confirming both quality and authenticity. A certified stone offers clarity, confidence, and peace of mind throughout the purchasing process.</p><p>At WILLIAM ÉDOUARD, every diamond is carefully sourced with full traceability, selected exclusively from trusted, vetted suppliers and responsibly mined in alignment with the Kimberley Process. This ensures each stone is ethically sourced and conflict-free. Over time, strong relationships have been built with respected suppliers known for producing exceptional gem-quality diamonds.</p><p>Many diamonds and gemstones are discreetly laser-inscribed, often with a unique identifier, using technology invisible to the naked eye. This marking, viewable under magnification with a jeweller’s loupe, serves as a final assurance of authenticity and reflects the rigorous standards each stone must meet before being selected.</p>",
            "heading_size_desktop": 30,
            "text_size_desktop": 18,
            "padding_left_desktop": 380,
            "padding_right_desktop": 380,
